            "s1",
            "s2",
            "s3"
          ],
          "tier": "B",
          "authority_label": "fact"
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "field": "release.chase_structure",
          "text": "The local catalog's attention rows include Dark Blastoise, Dark Charizard, Dark Gyarados, Dark Dragonite, Dark Raichu, and holo Trainer cards such as Here Comes Team Rocket! and Rocket's Sneak Attack.",
          "sources": [
            "s1"
          ],
          "tier": "B",
          "authority_label": "local_catalog_fact"
        },
        {
          "id": "c7",
          "field": "artist.impact",
          "text": "The local catalog's credited-artist clusters for Team Rocket are led by Kagemaru Himeno, Mitsuhiro Arita, Ken Sugimori, Sumiyoshi Kizuki, and Atsuko Nishida.",
          "sources": [
            "s1"
          ],
          "tier": "B",
          "authority_label": "local_catalog_fact"
        },
        {
          "id": "c8",
          "field": "history.significance",
          "text": "Team Rocket matters because it turns the binder into a moral weather system: familiar Generation I creatures are reintroduced through ownership, neglect, and villain framing, while the checklist itself hides a structural wink in Dark Raichu's 83/82 numbering.",
